New route in `routes/products.js`, alongside the existing paged listing:

```js
router.get("/search", async (req, res) => {
  const rows = await db.query(
    `SELECT id, sku, name, price_cents,
            ts_rank(search_vector, query) AS rank
     FROM products, websearch_to_tsquery('english', $1) query
     WHERE active AND search_vector @@ query
     ORDER BY rank DESC LIMIT 50`,
    [req.query.q]
  );
  res.json(rows);
});
```

`websearch_to_tsquery` is the one worth picking deliberately — it parses plain user input (multi-word, quotes, `-exclude`) safely, unlike `to_tsquery` which needs pre-formatted operator syntax.

Left out: this stems and matches on words, so it won't catch typos or partial substrings ("wdiget" for "widget") — that needs `pg_trgm` layered in later if users complain. Not needed at this scale otherwise.

